# FireSight frontend environment — copy to `.env` and adjust as needed.
#
# Expo (SDK 57) inlines every EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable into the bundle at build
# time. Restart `expo start` after changing this file.
#
# Base URL of the FireSight FastAPI backend. Leave unset to use the deployed
# production backend:
#   https://firesight-backend-2rm4.onrender.com
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT — point the app at your local FastAPI server instead
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web browser or iOS simulator:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
#
# Android emulator (10.0.2.2 is Android's alias for the host loopback):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:8000
#
# PHYSICAL PHONE TESTING: on a real device 127.0.0.1 refers to the phone
# itself, so point this at your computer's LAN IP instead (find it with
# `ipconfig` on Windows / `ifconfig` on macOS), for example:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.100:8000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Map screen notes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WEB MAP — Leaflet + OpenStreetMap tiles (free, no key, no billing).
# Address search uses OpenStreetMap's Nominatim (also free, no key).
#
# NATIVE MAP — react-native-maps (Google Maps on Android, Apple Maps on
# iOS). Expo Go ships a temporary Google Maps key for development. For a
# STANDALONE Android build (eas build / prebuild), add your own key in
# app.json under: expo.android.config.googleMaps.apiKey
# iOS needs no key (Apple Maps).
#
# NO provider keys (NASA FIRMS, WFIGS, Open-Meteo) belong here — the app
# only ever talks to the FireSight backend above.
